  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sea Turtle Rescue and Conservation in Playa Grande</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Playa Grande, Cahuita is home to three unique species of marine turtles: critically endangered Hawksbill and Leatherbacks and endangered Caribbean Green turtles.  The area is home to terrestrial species, such as green iguanas, howler monkeys and coatis. Cahuita Turtle Rescue leads community-based conservation efforts such as beach cleans, nest harvesting, turtle releases and educational campaigns to ensure the survival of the marine turtle population and protect their rights to survive and nest.</narrative>
  </description>
